-- Mini Myths event archive -> BattlePack
-- Generated by tools/minimyths-ingest/transform/gen_sql.py — do not hand-edit.
--
-- 89 packs, 92 segments, 133 schedule items, 133 category rows.
--
-- Idempotent. Every row is guarded, and pack ids are derived (uuid5) from the
-- Notion page id, so applying this twice changes nothing the second time.
--
-- Segment 1 is UPDATED, not inserted. battlepacks_create_first_segment is an
-- AFTER INSERT trigger that always creates ordinal 1 from the pack's date
-- columns, so those ARE written here and the auto-created segment is then
-- corrected (ends_at, label, and ends_on for a two-day pack, whose segment 1
-- is one day only). Inserting segment 1 instead would collide on
-- (pack_id, ordinal) or silently skip and leave a dateless segment.
--
-- Items store DURATION, not clock times: migration 20260728010000 dropped
-- starts_at/ends_at from items, so every clock time is derived from the
-- anchor plus the durations before it. The chain is contiguous and replays
-- to the source times exactly; the 6 gaps the sources state (changeover and
-- pre-awards packup) are their own break items rather than being absorbed
-- into the preceding round, which would misstate its length.
--
-- Schedule items omit segment_id on purpose: battlepack_item_default_segment
-- fills it with the pack's lowest-ordinal segment, which is where every
-- imported timetable belongs. That avoids depending on a trigger-generated id.
--
-- No notification is sent: notify_battlepack_segment_change() returns early
-- unless the pack has a row in battlepack_calendar_adds, and a new pack has
-- none. Verified before generating this.
--
-- Run as a role that bypasses RLS (service_role / postgres).

begin;

